cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Chalkline: California educator credential authorizations, modeled onto CTDL"
abstract: >-
  An unofficial worked example of California educator credential authorizations
  expressed in the Credential Transparency Description Language, built only from
  what the California Commission on Teacher Credentialing already publishes on its
  public Authorization Sort Table and credential leaflets. 133 authorizations are
  modeled as ceterms:License with their authorized subjects as subject alignments,
  validated against a vendored CTDL schema encoding with a recorded retrieval hash.
  Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or published by the Commission or by Credential
  Engine, and nothing in it has been published to the Credential Registry.
authors:
  - family-names: Kelly-Reif
    given-names: Chelsea
# `version` mirrors the in-development version in pyproject.toml, which is the single
# source of truth; tests/test_release_claims.py asserts the two agree. `date-released`
# is deliberately absent: no git tag and no GitHub Release exist for this project, and a
# citation manager prints that field as the date the software was released. The same test
# ties its presence to a tag naming the declared version, in both directions, so it comes
# back when a release is actually cut and not before.
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/chalkline"
url: "https://chelseakr.github.io/chalkline/"
type: software
keywords:
  - CTDL
  - credential-transparency
  - JSON-LD
  - linked-data
  - educator-credentials
  - open-data
